  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-06-19T15:22:36.230Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For Physics.Raycast, you need to define a mask. But using LayerMask.GetMask(\"MaskName\") will result into a strange situation where your code works in Unity but not in the VRChat client. There is no error message or log indicating that this function failed. The only way to get a working mask is to define it as int mask = 0b00000001_00000000_00000000_00000000; for mask with index 24 and so on. \n\nSince this function isn't working, it would be better to not have it exposed until it works, since this will just result into hours of \"why is my code not working\"-suffering.",
